{
  "fields_dropped": [
    "case_outcome_label",
    "case_outcome_score",
    "llm_case_outcome",
    "raw_result.summary.decision"
  ],
  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "3a7d1e041789497aa12abd4e0b6adb91_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "15. This being a criminal case, the burden of proving guilt of accused lies upon the prosecution for which the standard required is beyond reasonable doubt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "65ea640fa34f4ca5b5ff8d41a4c701db_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The accused persons in the present case have been charged with offence punishable under Section 304A IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a4cd0519b91243ab9c4cf84aa7086aa6_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The said provision deals with the death caused by negligence and consists of two components."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6270b8ea91c04fa9ba2fcdd435f54740_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The first is that death should be caused of the victim and the second is that the said death should be caused out of rash or negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7bd73407ecc64594b558b7c1114694c3_90",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Hon'ble Apex Court in the case titled as Ambalal D.\nBhatt Vs. State of Gujarat (1972) 3 SCC 525 has held as follows:-\n\"8."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4ab3409db2f14c74bee5a4807442add2_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It appears to us that in a prosecution for an offence under Section 304A, the mere fact that an accused contravenes certain rules or regulations in the doing of an act which causes death of another, does not establish that the death was the"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "17a63e07c6f54ebaae8381ff44e9ee6c_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If that were so, the acquittal of the appellant for contravention of the provisions of the Act and the Rules would itself have been an answer and we would have then examined to what extent additional evidence of his acquittal would have to "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b15aa04be0924bbe81d99fe40780f378_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As observed by Sir Lawrence Jenkins in Emperor v. Omkar Rampratap (1902) 4 Bom LR 679 the act causing the deaths \"must be the cause causans; It is not enough that it may have been the causa sine qua non\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f1e35a14133245778235e3be66b6c871_94",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This view has been adopted by this Court in State vs Sibasish Paul Etc on 5 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/117933791/\n4 several decisions."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4080cf1aed21406c85524a01b0530b2e_95",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Kurban Hussein Moham-medali Rangwala v. State of Maharashtra, the accused who had manufactured wet paints without a licence was acquitted of the charge under Section 304A because it was held that the mere fact that he allowed the burners"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ab482af728ed41d5b5315785b5a02b98_96",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The cause of the fire was not merely the presence of the burners within the room in which varnish and turpentine were stored though this circumstance was indirectly responsible for the fire which broke out, but was also due to the overflowi"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "70c7d63802c64e9e9cbe938a31d1447c_97",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Suieman Rahiman Mulani v. State of Maharashtra the accused who was driving a car only with a learner's licence without a trainer by his side, had injured a person."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b3fb555aefa6487986ebd13d823dc04b_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was held that that by itself was not sufficient to warrant a conviction under Section 304A.\n"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "11b15e9892b54381999c6c451703ebee_99",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It would"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f955985717df4761a370c0793c49024f_100",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "be different if it can be established as in the case of Bhalchandra v. State of Maharashtra that deaths and injuries caused by the contravention of a prohibition in respect of the substances which are highly dangerous as in the case of expl"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e383ebec7247469ebdf818a84757430b_101",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": ", that contravention would be the causa causans.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "81d0cd9069cf473fb6ee9968ad2585b5_102",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHence, it was held that the alleged rash and negligent act should have very close proximity with the factum of death suffered by the victim without the intervention of any third party."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6f5ea7ad19f947e8a7606ac4ff7ffa38_103",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The death should have been the direct result of the rash and negligent act of the accused and the act must be proximate and efficient cause without the intervention of anyone else's negligence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "16f19144f4ac45e3b389652e408d1174_104",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Hence, it is a settled proposition of law that it is not sufficient to show that the death in question was caused due to any act of the accused but it also needs to be established that the said act was the immediate or proximate cause of th"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "54c4b8516869433e880dcb94407ee268_105",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the present case, PW1 is the independent eye-witness who deposed that the victim was electrocuted while he was playing on the sign board."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6de6786e51c0453d910baa018387258c_106",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, in his cross-examination, he has stated that he did not see the child/victim climbing or sitting on the sign board."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b4066cf1489042ba841255b36b5f4373_107",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Further, perusal of the photographs of the concerned sign board Ex. P1 (colly) shows that there is no place for a child to play on the said board."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f7ab6ea93226436bbd7ae5133045ddc5_108",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Hence, it is not clear as to what was the manner in which the victim came into contact with the live wire allegedly running through the sign board."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fa33a81b1bbc4cfa9ae49a652daf5cf7_109",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "PW3 i.e. the mother of the victim is another eye-witness examined by the prosecution who has also not deposed regarding the manner in which the victim touched the live wire causing him to receive electric shock."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "10babf1bad7a4267aa581f9e87c26077_110",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "She has deposed that \"he somehow touched the portion of the wire, which was not insulated and was electrocuted and got stuck with he wire.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "17267e96fb8c4f11859075f71c60ad04_111",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "From the said testimony a sufficient doubt has been raised pointing out towards the contributory negligence on the part of the victim and his guardian who was present at the spot."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "26b9a00d89cb4f41a9eee015bd52ef64_112",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is also not clear whether the electrocution occurred due to the manipulation of the wire by the child or whether it was uninsulated on the date of the accident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3910724c6bf04650adc03b0af1f7af06_113",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "17. Regarding the examination of the wires in question that were supposed to be installed on the advertisement board, the prosecution has examined PW5, PW6 and PW12."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d72ede81c5774eeebd09e8940e73622a_114",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "PW5 has deposed that on 11.02.2003, he alongwith PW6 went to PS CP upon instructions of the Electrical Inspector i.e. PW12."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "15f33ec76a78436e8f95f0c1cf90febb_115",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "State vs Sibasish Paul Etc on 5 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/117933791/\n5"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "24b54004f33441d5b87b6267aa02df33_116",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On that day, the IO was not available and inspection of the wires was finally conducted on 12.03.2003."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2595dc202e6345dcab3b605245431966_117",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Both PW5 & PW6 have deposed on the same lines and have opined that there was sparking due to short circuit as live copper conductor in the wire came in contact with the iron angle of the sign board."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bef5af213b074b8dae3c06938ebd0b34_118",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was also observed that the PVC insulation upon the wire was damaged in various places."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "58cb78b927a944c18b93caf4e77b91b8_119",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is pertinent to note that the incident in question occurred on 03.02.2003 while the inspection and examination of the wires was conducted on 12.03.2003 which is more than one month after the incident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "853f6b22ee034c21b9fd585c59a8dc60_120",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This creates a doubt regarding the condition of the wires in question at the time of the incident as objects in general are susceptible to general wear and tear due to passage of time."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "52aecec23c264d9a89a511187d265cde_121",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The prosecution has not been able to prove beyond reasonable doubt as to whether the wires in question had not been properly insulated at the time of incident itself."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7b909c4e1aef4567b6badcf8ded974da_122",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "PW13 who is the IO has deposed that he took the wires in possession from the spot and clicked photographs of the same."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "aef1d97f97154c099f3fcd9c35b69ac4_123",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHowever, perusal of the said photographs show that they are not close enough to reveal whether the PVC insulation was not present at multiple places upon the wire."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "31114f99a1c34ec8a43866757f7a22eb_124",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The safe custody of the electric wires after their seizure from the spot has also not been sufficiently proved."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "aa73c11299ad4f1e932ce1978c05e6f0_125",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n18. It has been argued on behalf of the prosecution that the death of the victim due to electrocution itself reveals that the wires on the advertisement on the Metlife Insurance installed at the spot were not properly insulated."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ce3922d54f844f4ab4fcbd35a0234331_126",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In this regard, reference has been made to the doctrine of res ipsa loquitur."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "04b3e059626e413287abd4b22e1c576e_127",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHowever, the Hon'ble Supreme Court in case titled as Syad Akbar vs. State of Karnataka 1979 Cri LJ 1374 has held that the aforesaid doctrine would not apply to a criminal case in the strict sense."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dc882688ffac4d638a143d779aec8370_128",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The following observations were made in this regard."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b2757f22966e44779755b8ff3b106980_129",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n\"Such simplified and pragmatic application of the notion of res ipsa loquitur, as a part of the general mode of inferring a fact in issue from another circumstantial fact,\nis subject to all the principles, the satisfaction of which is esse"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "21bcf8d1efc14ea1b0906f9fcfce47e5_130",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Those are: Firstly, all the circumstances, including the objective circumstances constituting the accident,\nfrom which the inference of guilt is to be drawn, must be firmly established."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "516979ef528c438badf0cd50415ccd62_131",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nSecondly, those circumstances must be of a determinative tendency pointing unerringly towards the guilt of the accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fad479a20558453a9a722dca876ebf0d_132",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thirdly, the circumstances should make a chain so complete that they cannot reasonably raise any other hypothesis save that of the accused's guilt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5426a347fd64472ca9e16bbfa913e988_133",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "That is to say, they should be incompatible with his innocence,\nand inferentially exclude all reasonable doubt about his guilt.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4eb56fa543684fc9b9ec2f6e075fd84a_134",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHence, in order to apply the doctrine of res ipsa loquitur, it is essential to demonstrate a complete chain of circumstances beginning from the commission of the negligent act by the accused to the resulting death."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d2062c3dd21d40c7b5fda04757f653e6_135",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The prosecution in the present case has alleged that both the accused persons were responsible for the safe keeping or maintenance of the wires installed in the sign board at the spot."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a08167ece7754e2d8822892c1b0852ee_136",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Both the eye-witnesses PW1 & PW3 have not deposed regarding the culpability or responsibility of the accused persons."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7d462da941384d5e8049b9c9346a4ee2_137",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Hence, it was the duty of the investigating agency to find out as to who was the person responsible for the safe keeping of the premises where the incident occurred."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1c9568d68be049329bfb8a3d44e5e095_138",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It has been submitted on behalf of the prosecution that accused Jitender Kumar was the contractor for the electricity supply of the subway (premises in question) and accused Sibashish Paul was the structure Engineer of Selvel Media Pvt. Ltd"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "90c272c126bd43caaa7ff8ca3c7046a0_139",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nState vs Sibasish Paul Etc on 5 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/117933791/\n6 19."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d11fae34ce384398924f22086808cfab_140",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "From the perusal of the entire record, it is not clear as to what led to the inference that it was the accused persons who were responsible for regular safe keeping of the premises."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a00aa18617a94d32ae6415a7e173c797_141",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The IO PW13 in his cross-examination stated that he has no idea whether any inspection was done by the NDMC prior to the incident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "543f8ae1cb474eee842936edcd99ee2e_142",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This leads to a conclusion that no investigation was conducted regarding the role of NDMC in the safe keeping of the electrical wires present at the spot."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c8c5551df2a2481a966efac767babc9b_143",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The IO has further stated in his cross-examination that he did not collect any document regarding the maintenance of the subway and also did not collect any document to show that any of the accused was the contractor of the electrical work "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5f2bc9ab414347c9b87b27078bb78207_144",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is no document to show the date on which any contract was given to the accused Jitender Kumar regarding the electrical supply to the subway."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "813d8d3dc5f64223a5984a91d2fb6fac_145",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Further, there is no document to show the exact role of the contractor or the structure engineer in maintaining the electrical wires due to which the incident occurred."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d28211665e2a4486b2a0f609b210464a_146",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Even if it is assumed for a moment that the accused persons were infact responsible for installing the wires in question, there is no documentary or oral evidence to show that both the accused persons were directly responsible for regular i"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e3d2bf46696441cea00610da0ed953c1_147",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHence, the chain of events required to prove the offence punishable under Section 304A IPC has not been established by the prosecution."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "52c2849d99bb4443ba9a0390a8de80e4_148",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "20. In view of the above discussion, this court is therefore, of the view that the prosecution has failed to establish its case beyond reasonable doubt, benefit of which must accrue to the accused persons."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e5be5090cea24b3484096eb1088f94bf_149",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAccordingly, both accused persons namely Sibashish Paul and Jitender Kumar Sharma are acquitted of the offence punishable under Section 304A IPC."
    }
  ],
